1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:14,120
 Le temps est écoulé, oui, pour la période de questions. Parfait. Merci beaucoup.

2
00:00:28,120 --> 00:00:31,300
 Il restait deux questions en personne.

3
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:34,300
 On va faire l'extension de 15 minutes, puis on va les laisser.

4
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:35,780
 Pardon?

5
00:00:36,360 --> 00:00:37,220
 En présentiel.

6
00:00:37,460 --> 00:00:40,340
 Il reste deux questions. Il reste M. Rappaport et M. Jass.

7
00:00:41,720 --> 00:00:42,600
 On va les prendre, alors.

8
00:00:44,560 --> 00:00:49,880
 Avec l'extension, on va voter une prolongation pour entendre les deux dernières personnes présentes.

9
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:52,500
 Oui, M. Moreau le propose, Mme Tia-Garaja l'appuie.

10
00:00:53,360 --> 00:00:53,640
 Merci.

11
00:00:56,240 --> 00:01:05,500
 Irwin, you can go ahead, please, and ask your question.

12
00:01:11,420 --> 00:01:24,680
 As some of the councillors are aware, the Terre-Bun bike path was imposed...

13
00:01:24,680 --> 00:01:26,640
 Oh, sorry. Thank you.

14
00:01:30,680 --> 00:01:41,940
 The Terre-Bun bike path was imposed by Projet-Moriel without a proper public consultation, even though Peter McQueen says that the consultation was the election in 2021.

15
00:01:43,940 --> 00:01:47,120
 This bike path was a flood...

16
00:01:47,120 --> 00:01:55,200
 The EXP study was flawed, and it's well-known by Councillor Moroz and yourself, Mayor Valenzuela.

17
00:01:55,200 --> 00:02:08,460
 The bike path should have been closed last winter, but it wasn't, so I would welcome closing the bike path even one lane this winter.

18
00:02:08,460 --> 00:02:23,720
 What we're asking for is that the Borough do a proper consultation in which every resident of NDG has an opportunity to provide information on what they feel about the bike path.

19
00:02:23,720 --> 00:02:39,980
 It could be three or four public meetings, it could be a bilingual website where people could submit their thoughts on the bike path, and we could have four or five options where people could vote for it.

20
00:02:39,980 --> 00:02:56,240
 One could be eliminating the bike path, one could be eliminating the bike path, one could be having a bike path between Madison and Girouard, one could be having one bidirectional lane from Belmore to Girouard.

21
00:02:56,240 --> 00:02:59,240
 It could be four or five explained options.

22
00:02:59,240 --> 00:03:04,920
 The point is, this bike path, you know the problems associated with this bike path.

23
00:03:04,920 --> 00:03:14,780
 It removed more than 350 parking spots that Peter McQueen says, "Oh, that's not a problem, we have 13,000, 14,000 parking spots in NDG."

24
00:03:15,840 --> 00:03:27,620
 It causes more traffic to go on the side streets, it increases greenhouse gas emissions, it's a problem for fire trucks, for garbage collection trucks,

25
00:03:29,160 --> 00:03:38,020
 it's a problem for the schools, which you guys well know, it's a problem for the seniors residents, it was a problem for the church.

26
00:03:38,020 --> 00:03:51,020
 So what I'm asking is, can this borough hold a proper bilingual public consultation, which would include a website, a vote for suggestions on the future of the bike path,

27
00:03:51,020 --> 00:03:57,880
 so that we could get a proper idea of how the residents feel, and make a decision based on that.

28
00:03:57,880 --> 00:04:06,880
 Because people have been opposing, we had over three and a half thousand signatures that we submitted here and downtown, against the bike path.

29
00:04:06,880 --> 00:04:13,740
 And closing the bike path for three months in the year and retaining it is, it's an insult.

30
00:04:13,740 --> 00:04:23,740
 It means that the Project Montréal project is supported by Ensemble, which is offensive, and it's just not right.

31
00:04:23,740 --> 00:04:31,740
 So, will you agree to hold a proper bilingual public consultation so the residents can have their say?

32
00:04:31,740 --> 00:04:35,840
 Thank you so much, Erwin, for coming to council, thank you for your question.

33
00:04:35,840 --> 00:04:48,700
 I think it's really important for me to reiterate that we're the third administration to have to take a decision on the Taoban bike path.

34
00:04:48,860 --> 00:04:53,860
 In 2020, it was first put in place, and after a couple of months, it was completely dismantled,

35
00:04:54,180 --> 00:05:00,480
 and a committee was put in place to have recommendations with members that were for the bike path and against the bike path.

36
00:05:00,480 --> 00:05:06,440
 And Mr. McQueen even sat on that committee, and those recommendations were very, very clear.

37
00:05:06,940 --> 00:05:12,480
 It's important to go back to the entire, you know, history of the file.

38
00:05:13,260 --> 00:05:16,840
 So, in 2020, there were clear testimonies.

39
00:05:16,980 --> 00:05:19,520
 There was even, like, an ombudsman report that came from it.

40
00:05:19,640 --> 00:05:25,840
 And last year, not last year, but in the last mandate, there was also an ombudsman report that came out on the bike path

41
00:05:25,840 --> 00:05:29,840
 with regards to the implementation of it through the previous administration.

42
00:05:30,480 --> 00:05:40,340
 So, there's petitions that have been deposed at multiple instances in favor of it, against it, with high numbers on both ends.

43
00:05:40,880 --> 00:05:48,200
 There was an information session that was disguised as a consultation process in the last administration as well,

44
00:05:48,280 --> 00:05:53,760
 where over 400 people clearly came in this same room in November, November 30th,

45
00:05:53,760 --> 00:05:57,440
 to share their various opinions on the project.

46
00:05:57,440 --> 00:06:10,460
 And Sunny and myself really sat in the last mandate and heard every single testimony or opinion or experience.

47
00:06:10,900 --> 00:06:17,200
 So, I understand that many people would like us to put a hold, again, on the process that we've put in place

48
00:06:17,200 --> 00:06:23,060
 because they want us to restart an entire process that our administration believes has been done

49
00:06:23,060 --> 00:06:26,860
 in many iterations at many instances in the last six years.

50
00:06:27,320 --> 00:06:29,720
 So, again, thank you so much for coming to our council meeting.

51
00:06:29,860 --> 00:06:31,980
 Thank you for sharing your request.

52
00:06:31,980 --> 00:06:42,620
 But I think at this point, with regards to our proposition, it's something that we believe, again, is a juste milieu, it's a compromise.

53
00:06:43,400 --> 00:06:48,900
 And we believe that this is something that will be able to respond to the many needs of our residents.

54
00:06:49,100 --> 00:06:50,700
 If I could just raise one quick point.

55
00:06:50,960 --> 00:06:51,180
 Yes.

56
00:06:52,720 --> 00:07:01,640
 The support that Councillor Moroze and yourself gave for democracy and the lack of consultation was very much appreciated.

57
00:07:03,080 --> 00:07:06,220
 We still have an opportunity to do the right thing.

58
00:07:07,040 --> 00:07:11,300
 This bike path, Terrebonne was safe for cyclists for decades.

59
00:07:11,980 --> 00:07:14,700
 There's been very few incidents on Terrebonne.

60
00:07:14,940 --> 00:07:16,960
 And none are reported in the press.

61
00:07:17,200 --> 00:07:18,420
 I've done a search for that.

62
00:07:19,100 --> 00:07:26,840
 So, what we're asking for is simply to keep the bike path as is temporarily.

63
00:07:27,620 --> 00:07:34,240
 Hold a proper public consultation where the residents of NDG can have their say.

64
00:07:34,340 --> 00:07:36,440
 Because this is, we lost a thoroughfare.

65
00:07:37,520 --> 00:07:39,740
 This bike path causes delays.

66
00:07:40,460 --> 00:07:47,000
 It puts more traffic on the side streets where children and seniors are.

67
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:50,580
 It puts more traffic on Monkland and Summerled.

68
00:07:51,340 --> 00:07:53,160
 There's a lot of problems with this bike path.

69
00:07:53,360 --> 00:08:01,500
 And EXP did a flawed study in which they only studied the area for two days and didn't ask the right questions.

70
00:08:02,460 --> 00:08:11,340
 So, if you have, if we can keep the bike path as is and do a proper study where NDG residents have their say,

71
00:08:11,440 --> 00:08:24,140
 that would be greatly appreciated, would this council be willing to do, to hold such a referent, public consultation to get the, to understand the true nature and views of the residents?

72
00:08:24,480 --> 00:08:29,460
 Whatever the solution is and whatever people's, whatever the majority says.

73
00:08:29,780 --> 00:08:32,500
 Thank you again, Irwin, for your proposition.

74
00:08:32,840 --> 00:08:36,440
 But I think our administration has been very clear with where we want to go on the bike path.

75
00:08:36,840 --> 00:08:37,400
 Thank you.

76
00:08:37,620 --> 00:08:38,020
 Thank you.

77
00:08:42,520 --> 00:08:43,380
 Steven Jass.

78
00:08:43,640 --> 00:08:44,180
 Mr. Jass.

79
00:08:44,180 --> 00:09:00,000
 Mr. Jass.

